{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/250359-fan-made-seattle-material","id":250359,"title":"Fan-made Seattle Material?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-05T20:23:26-07:00","id":250359,"title":"Fan-made Seattle Material?","content":"What stuff have you guys added to the Splintered City for your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T13:44:00-07:00","id":256216,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is the sort of thing you're looking for, but my campaign's home city hosts possible future splinters, making it a counterpoint to the base setting as Seattle. I'm grafting on the State:Machine and Fear Tomorrow shards as soon as the Storyteller's guide comes out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T09:08:07-07:00","id":261285,"title":"","content":"I added a facility to Seattle University in my game. The purpose of the facility was to house, guard and maintain a relic and a captive demon that was being interrogated regarding the relic by angels. These angels fell.<br /> <br /> Other things I've done with Seattle is I changed up the vampires to include the Holy Engineers and decided that the vampires of Seattle are in a pickle, as their Prince suffered radio sickness and has since joined the Holy Engineers, giving that rather esoteric and small-time covenant a new-found huge amount of power in the city. This has forced a sort of vampire-secret-police scenario on the remaining covenants who are forced to congregate in secret away from mainstay vampire society.<br /> <br /> Needless to say my players' ring are investigating the possibilities that this turn of events presents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}